.TH LINEAR 1 2000-1月 "elastic_net" "elastic_net"
.SH NAME
elastic_net \- Fit a linear (elastic net) gene regulatory network from the expression matrix.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIelastic_net(\fBx\fR as <generic> Matrix, 
\fBcandidates\fR as integer = 300, 
\fBmaxreg\fR as integer = 10, 
\fBl1_ratio\fR as double = 0.7, 
\fBalphas\fR as double = 20, 
\fBmutual\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBTF\fR as any = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBpriority\fR as any = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBregulators\fR as any = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBstandardize\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBmin_abs_r\fR as double = 0, 
\fBgpu\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBblock_screener\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBpartial_correlation\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBpartial_cond\fR as integer = 5, 
\fBnegative_quota\fR as integer = -1, 
\fBmax_row_sum\fR as double = 0.9, 
\fBpriority_budget\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBthreads\fR as integer = -1);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Fit a linear (elastic net) gene regulatory network from the expression matrix.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBx\fB \fR\- the gene expression matrix, rows are genes and columns are samples. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcandidates\fB \fR\- 
 the max number of the candidate regulators for each target gene, the candidates
 are picked by the absolute pearson correlation with the target gene.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmaxreg\fB \fR\- the max number of the non-zero regulation edges that each target gene can keep. 
.PP
.PP
\fBl1_ratio\fB \fR\- the L1 mixing ratio of the elastic net, in the range [0, 1]. 
.PP
.PP
\fBalphas\fB \fR\- the number of the alpha steps in the regularization path. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmutual\fB \fR\- only keep the reversible (mutual) regulation pairs. 
.PP
.PP
\fBTF\fB \fR\- 
 an optional gene id vector of the transcript factors, these genes are always
 included in the candidate regulator pool (they are not affected by the
 **candidates** truncation). Non TF genes are still able to be the
 regulators, so that the knockdown of a non TF gene still has downstream responses.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBstandardize\fB \fR\- z-score the expression vectors before the fitting. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmin_abs_r\fB \fR\- the minimal absolute pearson correlation for a gene to be a candidate regulator. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a list object with two slots: \fBgrn\fR (the fitted [GeneRegulatoryNetwork](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Model.Network.Regulons.LinearRegression.GeneRegulatoryNetwork))
 and \fBedges\fR (the [RegulationEdge](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Model.Network.Regulons.LinearRegression.RegulationEdge) collection).
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
linear
.SH FILES
.PP
TRNtoolkit.dll
.PP
